WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is so lovely to see you.
-What happened, Seth?

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.204
-I know. Well, we have known
each other for a very long time.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.272 size:75% position:38%
-We were hanging out
in our 20s together.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were.
-And now I look up,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're on the cover
of "Time" magazine.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like -- What happened?
-Yeah, a lot happened.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.512 line:92%
Because we were in our 20s.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
We weren't doing much
that you would have thought

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be on any magazine.
-No, I was positive

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.917
you would never be on the
cover of "Time" magazine.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was like some
police-blotter [bleep],

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.655
I would say, more than anything.
-Yeah, there was some stuff.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you --
You hosted "SNL" in 2005.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:26.659
That's when we got to know
each other. You had a place.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.162
You had a really nice apartment
in New York.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I decided
to move to New York

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I had such a great week
hosting "SNL"

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.301 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and I shot a movie here.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:39.105
And then I had --
This is the greatest thing ever.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.208 size:78% position:39%
You move to New York.
I invited Seth over.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Hey,
can I bring some friends?"

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was like
half the cast of "SNL."

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:49.049
-Yeah, when anybody with a nice
apartment invited us over,

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to bring
everybody we knew.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just couldn't get --
My first night in New York,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:57.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's, like, Amy Poehler
is doing impressions.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.124 line:92%
I had, like, a karaoke machine.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:02.562
Horatio Sanz is doing, like,
his Elton John impression.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was scream-singing
Elton John.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was like, you know,
"Welcome to New York.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is the dream."

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:11.104
And then like a month or two
later, I saw you at a party,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was with, like,
a platonic girlfriend of mine.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "Oh, my God.
I have the biggest
crush on Seth Meyers."

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.380
I'm like, "I know him. I hosted
'SNL.' I know this guy."

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we went over
to say hi to you,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.885
and you were really nice to her,
and then you said,

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:29.322
"By the way, Topher, you were,
like, the greatest host ever."

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, well,
I mean, maybe for the season,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.229
but not for, like, the whole --
Not ever."

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:40.300
And you go, "Oh, my God. No, I
meant at your house that time.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were actually not
that good a host at 'SNL.'"

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I value one so much higher
than the other.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, man,
congratulations on this movie.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-It's fantastic.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.383
The reviews are wonderful.
And you had not an easy task.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for those
who haven't seen this film,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is a strange lightness
to this story.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.326 size:88% position:44%
I mean, it's really told
in a really unique way.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.227 line:92%
But you have to play this,

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, horrifying person,
David Duke.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And there are times

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I would imagine
it's intimidating enough

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
working with a director
like Spike Lee,

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:19.005
but he would give you notes
on how to perform David Duke.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.575
-Yeah, just taking the role
and the research I had to do --

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've done research
on roles before,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this was, like,
the worst research imaginable.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.183
So it was, like, a terrible
month, and then I showed up,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we did all
the Klan rally stuff first.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is why you
have to work with a great
director like Spike Lee.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
he kind of takes care of you

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.094
and makes you feel better,
but every once in a while, he --

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know this --
In comedy films,

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.630 size:75% position:38% line:92%
he'll kind of run in

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.465 size:81% position:41%
and give you something
to improv at the end.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, at the end of the scene
or if they have an idea,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll kind of whisper
something in your ear and say,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.105
"Try throwing that in,"
so none of the actors will know

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
about it, none of the crew
or anything.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:59.746
And on this film, Spike
would run in and say in my ear,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:03.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, the most racist thing
I'd ever heard.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.054
And I'd go, "Hey, man, like,
no need to whisper it to me.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:11.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I don't want the credit
when I say it."

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:22.101
The whole crew is like, "Uh,
did Topher come up with that?"

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:22.869 line:92%
So I made him announce it.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:27.006
I was like, "I'll repeat what
you said to the entire crew."

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you --
I know you watched --

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
you listened to early radio
of David Duke,

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.312 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you watched old video.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When I got the call --
Spike Lee called me himself.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:38.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "You're my guy."
It's great day in your career.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.852
I could tell it was just
going to be a great movie.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I realize, "Oh,
this is going to be
worst month of my life."

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:48.094
I read his autobiography,
which is called "My Awakening."

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of like
his "Mein Kampf."

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.064 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's, like, horrible.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I watched
old filmed interviews.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.302
And there were actually some --
In the early '80s,

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
he did some episodes
of "Donahue."

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And that was where I really

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
drilled down
on what made him so evil.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:05.979
It was a studio audience like
this, and they all hated him.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.015
You know, he was the Grand
Wizard of the Ku Klux Klan.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.783 line:92%
So they're all booing at him.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.418 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And by the end of --

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't that
he flipped the crowd,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.321 line:92%
but by the end of the show,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.190 size:78% position:39%
they had a different
attitude towards him.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.326
I thought, "Oh, this guy is
truly evil in a really..."

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he has a charisma
about him.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.997
You know, that's a thing that...
-Yes.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.633
-...is the scariest in the hands
of the truly evil,

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.400 line:92%
is people are charismatic.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.136
But how do you even get your
hands on the David Duke book?

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well -- [ Laughs ]
That was, like, terrible.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.673 line:92%
First, I went to Barnes &amp; Noble.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't even thinking.
I was like...

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, I need 'My Awakening'
by David Duke."

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"Sorry. We don't carry that."

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.583 line:92%
And then I went on Amazon,

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:46.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
they ask you a couple times,

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:49.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "Did you mean
to order this thing?"

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.357 size:75% position:38%
And then since then,
I've been getting,

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, the weirdest
recommendations.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:05:00.600
You were also in a fantastic
Netflix film earlier this year,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
"War Machine" --
Or I guess last year now.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you got to
work with Brad Pitt.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:05.738 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah, I'm so excited.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.242
'Cause there is a little bit of
a buzz around "BlacKkKlansman."

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I made a deal
with Brad on the set.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.780
By the way, Brad didn't
want to hang out with me,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.647 line:92%
I'm sure, as much as he had to.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it all took place in the
desert, so it was like...

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.218 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-..."Sorry, man.
Just you and me."

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'd be in
a Black Hawk helicopter

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
for, like, you know,
the whole day.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, anyway,
after a long period of time,

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got the courage to ask him
what I wanted,

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was at
an Academy Award thing --

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:34.367
We don't go to the same parties,
me and Brad.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:37.236
But I was like, "If I get into
an Academy Award-type movie,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to be at that
"Vanity Fair" after-party,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.641 line:92%
and I want you to come up to me

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I'm talking
to someone important."

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.243 line:92%
He promised me he'd do this.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:47.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And be like,
"Topher, good to see you."

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to be like,
"Brad, not now."

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-This is your opportunity.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think "BlacKkKlansman"
is going to be it.

